OPEN-SOURCE REFERENCES & ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
================================================================================

agy-pulse is open-source software released under the MIT License. It builds
upon and draws inspiration, architectural ideas, and telemetry decoding
references from the following open-source projects:

1. zzusec/agy-statusline
   Repository: https://github.com/zzusec/agy-statusline
   Referenced concepts:
   - Real-time context window progress bar rendering
   - Protobuf server compaction ceiling decoding
   - Session cost monitoring and uppercase K/M token formatting style

2. icebear0828/agy-hud
   Repository: https://github.com/icebear0828/agy-hud
   Referenced concepts:
   - Multi-line Antigravity CLI HUD layout
   - Cloud quota panel visualization
   - Session telemetry structure

3. elviscjn-cjn/antigravity-context-viewer
   Repository: https://github.com/elviscjn-cjn/antigravity-context-viewer
   Referenced concepts:
   - gen_metadata Protobuf decoding for timeToFirstToken and streamingDuration
   - Per-model streaming output speed statistics
   - Model pricing rate alignment

